# Line-ending policy
#
# Evidence manifests and review records (gateware/**/manifest.json, cnc1/evidence/**,
# hardware/*.json, reports/*.json, research/*.json, firmware SHA256SUMS, ...) hash raw
# file bytes. This working tree mixes LF and CRLF files, and this host sets
# core.autocrlf=true system-wide, so any conversion on commit or checkout would change
# recorded hashes. The default is therefore: no end-of-line conversion at all. Every
# file is stored and checked out byte-for-byte on Windows, Linux and macOS clones.
# (-text only disables conversion; diff and merge still treat text files as text.)
* -text

# Sources that the documented WSL/Linux commands execute or parse must be LF
# (run_tests.sh, gateware/synthesis/run.sh, postmap/run.sh, LinuxCNC profiles,
# Yosys scripts, C/C++ built under WSL). Every such file is LF in the working tree,
# so normalising them does not change any recorded hash; a CRLF edit is converted
# back to LF instead of silently breaking the Linux reproduction.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.v text eol=lf
*.sv text eol=lf
*.ys text eol=lf
*.c text eol=lf
*.h text eol=lf
*.cpp text eol=lf
*.ini text eol=lf
*.hal text eol=lf
*.ngc text eol=lf
*.tbl text eol=lf
display-client text eol=lf
# *.py and *.hex deliberately follow the byte-exact default: several hashed Python
# tools and tests outside gateware/ are CRLF or mixed (for example
# tools/build_hardware_cost_data.py, tools/check_release.py, the tools/hardware_*
# scripts, tests/test_release.py and tools/build_compute_display_matrix.py), and an
# eol=lf rule would rewrite them on a fresh clone.
# More specific rules live beside the trees that need them: gateware/.gitattributes
# makes everything under gateware/ LF (its before-audit-fixes archives stay -text);
# cnc1/.gitattributes forces LF for its *.py, C/C++ and shell sources;
# controller_backend/.gitattributes covers only *.ini, *.hal, *.sh, *.ngc and
# display-client (it has no *.py rule).

# Binary artefacts.
*.so binary
*.o binary
*.a binary
*.elf binary
*.bin binary
*.pdf binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.xlsx binary
*.zip binary

# Large generated netlists: tracked because manifests hash them and the post-map flow
# consumes them, but not worth line diffs.
gateware/synthesis/results/cnc_endpoint_efinix.json -diff linguist-generated
gateware/synthesis/results/*.edif -diff linguist-generated
gateware/synthesis/postmap/results/mapped.v -diff linguist-generated
reports/root-verification-*/**/gateware/synthesis/results/cnc_endpoint_efinix.json -diff linguist-generated
reports/root-verification-*/**/gateware/synthesis/results/*.edif -diff linguist-generated
reports/root-verification-*/**/gateware/synthesis/postmap/results/mapped.v -diff linguist-generated
